WEBVTT

00:06.631 --> 00:08.633
[theme music playing]

00:15.265 --> 00:16.891
BASED ON THE KINGDOM OF THE GODS

00:22.647 --> 00:24.649
[suspenseful music playing]

00:58.850 --> 00:59.684
[clang]

01:39.057 --> 01:40.809
[owl hoots]

01:56.282 --> 01:57.242
[grunts]

01:59.828 --> 02:00.829
Your Royal Highness,

02:01.704 --> 02:03.248
why are you discarding this?

02:03.331 --> 02:05.291
After eating nothing but this for days,

02:06.126 --> 02:08.086
the mere sight of it makes me sick.

02:09.587 --> 02:10.755
[sighs]

02:10.839 --> 02:11.965
Exactly.

02:13.091 --> 02:15.593
Why did you do something so dangerous?

02:16.052 --> 02:17.303
You are reckless.

02:17.762 --> 02:19.472
You didn't need
to put yourself through this.

02:21.141 --> 02:23.017
I did not do it for my own sake.

02:24.144 --> 02:27.772
If I am dethroned, do you think
my personal guards will be safe?

02:28.189 --> 02:31.067
Your kind wife will also likely be killed.

02:31.901 --> 02:32.986
Exactly.

02:33.486 --> 02:35.405
You should not have schemed such a thing.

02:35.488 --> 02:38.158
You speak way too damn much.

02:38.241 --> 02:39.159
[sighs]

02:39.742 --> 02:42.495
Someone so noble like Your Royal Highness
should not say, "damn."

02:42.954 --> 02:45.331
Where did you pick up such a term?

02:45.415 --> 02:46.791
Where do you think?

02:47.458 --> 02:50.503
You are the only person around me
who speaks that way.

02:51.212 --> 02:52.046
I see.

02:52.463 --> 02:55.008
I must admit
that you are quite a fast learner--

02:55.091 --> 02:58.887
Oh, I must have been too nice to you.
You just do not know when to stop.

02:59.804 --> 03:03.391
Say one more word,
and I shall annihilate your entire family.

03:04.726 --> 03:05.810
[owl hoots]

03:11.441 --> 03:12.525
I said that in jest.

03:14.277 --> 03:15.236
Do not be angry.

03:16.529 --> 03:18.740
How could you jest
about something like that?

03:20.325 --> 03:24.454
How can the Crown Prince's personal guard
be so cowardly? You are useless.

03:24.996 --> 03:26.414
How could I not be afraid

03:26.497 --> 03:29.584
when the Crown Prince says
he would annihilate my family?

03:29.667 --> 03:30.710
[chuckles]

03:31.211 --> 03:32.545
Does this amuse you?

03:32.629 --> 03:33.880
[chortles]

03:33.963 --> 03:34.964
[chuckles]

03:35.465 --> 03:36.633
What's amusing about this?

03:36.716 --> 03:37.759
[laughs]

03:37.842 --> 03:38.801
Hmm?

03:39.761 --> 03:41.846
- [bird hoots]
- [laughing continues]

03:41.930 --> 03:43.932
[owl hoots]

03:45.225 --> 03:46.142
[sighs]

03:46.517 --> 03:47.852
Is this the right path?

03:49.437 --> 03:51.314
They told us
to head to Geumjeong Mountain.

03:51.773 --> 03:54.275
This is Geumjeong Mountain,
so we will get there soon.

03:54.359 --> 03:55.860
You said that before.

03:57.278 --> 03:59.530
If we do not arrive there in 30 minutes,

03:59.614 --> 04:01.574
I shall annihilate your family.

04:03.785 --> 04:06.829
Your Royal Highness,
do you truly enjoy jesting about that?

04:07.747 --> 04:08.915
I do.

04:09.374 --> 04:10.833
[laughs]

04:11.793 --> 04:12.627
[sighs]

04:12.710 --> 04:16.923
Keep jesting about annihilating my family
if it amuses you, Your Royal Highness.

04:17.799 --> 04:22.095
In return, please bestow me with seaweed
from Gijang if we survive.

04:22.178 --> 04:24.764
I hear that is the best
for pregnant women.

04:24.847 --> 04:26.599
I would appreciate some beef, too.

04:26.683 --> 04:28.101
[laughing]

04:29.560 --> 04:30.603
It is very odd.

04:31.229 --> 04:32.105
Pardon?

04:32.814 --> 04:33.815
Your Royal Highness,

04:33.898 --> 04:36.025
I left behind my pregnant wife
who is due any day now.

04:36.109 --> 04:39.237
Is it that odd of me to ask
for some seaweed from Gijang?

04:39.320 --> 04:40.530
That is not it.

04:41.739 --> 04:43.157
It is too quiet around here.

04:44.117 --> 04:46.494
I haven't heard an insect chirp
for a while now.

04:51.582 --> 04:53.584
[suspenseful music playing]

04:55.545 --> 04:57.714
[leaves rustling]

05:03.594 --> 05:04.595
Your Royal Highness,

05:05.847 --> 05:07.307
there is a house up ahead.

05:07.390 --> 05:08.308
[horse snorts]

05:12.145 --> 05:14.522
[ominous music playing]

05:14.605 --> 05:16.607
[horses trot]

05:22.822 --> 05:24.115
JIYULHEON

05:31.539 --> 05:33.666
I think this is the place,

05:34.542 --> 05:36.419
but it looks odd for a clinic.

05:36.502 --> 05:38.755
What is the blackish red thing
on the stake?

05:39.797 --> 05:41.299
Is that not blood?

05:45.094 --> 05:46.679
Wait here, Your Royal Highness.

06:04.238 --> 06:05.865
- [thud]
- [horse neighs]

06:15.625 --> 06:17.543
[wood rustling]

06:29.389 --> 06:30.473
Your Royal Highness,

06:31.057 --> 06:33.935
it is locked from the inside.
I shall climb over the wall.

06:50.868 --> 06:51.911
[soft thump]

06:57.375 --> 06:59.043
Mu-yeong, are you there?

07:02.463 --> 07:04.632
Is there a problem inside?

07:06.050 --> 07:07.260
Mu-yeong!

07:09.470 --> 07:10.555
Mu-yeong!

07:11.764 --> 07:13.182
Mu-yeong!

07:14.892 --> 07:16.853
[tense music playing]

07:33.619 --> 07:35.455
[ominous music playing]

07:51.345 --> 07:52.847
[clanks]

08:14.243 --> 08:16.162
I think something terrible happened

08:16.787 --> 08:18.873
to the people here.

08:18.956 --> 08:20.291
Where is Physician Lee Seung-hui?

08:21.042 --> 08:22.251
We came all this way.

08:22.752 --> 08:24.003
We must find him.

08:25.922 --> 08:27.131
Is anyone there?

08:29.634 --> 08:32.345
It is dangerous. Stay close to me,
Your Royal Highness.

08:36.224 --> 08:37.058
[grunts]

08:37.141 --> 08:39.310
Your Royal Highness! Are you all right?

08:40.061 --> 08:41.229
Are you hurt?

08:44.398 --> 08:46.192
[eerie music playing]

08:58.579 --> 08:59.580
[gasps]

09:27.984 --> 09:29.068
Pull!

09:29.777 --> 09:31.237
[soldiers grunting]

09:36.826 --> 09:38.077
[grunting continues]

09:39.370 --> 09:41.038
- Why is it so heavy?
- There are several.

09:41.122 --> 09:42.290
- What?
- Grab on!

09:43.499 --> 09:45.459
- [soldier] One, two!
- [soldiers grunt]

09:45.543 --> 09:47.253
- [soldier] One, two!
- [soldiers grunt]

09:47.712 --> 09:49.463
- [soldier] One, two!
- [soldiers grunt]

09:51.382 --> 09:52.967
[retching]

10:12.445 --> 10:15.489
[man] What brings a high military officer
all the way here from Hanyang?

10:15.906 --> 10:19.535
I heard Physician Lee Seung-hui was good,
so I wanted him to examine my brother.

10:21.537 --> 10:23.998
He looks fine, but he is not well.

10:24.081 --> 10:25.499
[indistinct chatter]

10:31.088 --> 10:32.131
[sighs]

10:32.590 --> 10:36.093
My brother rushed out and forgot
his identification. Please understand.

10:36.510 --> 10:37.595
I understand.

10:39.221 --> 10:43.059
Did you see anyone suspicious
when you arrived here?

10:43.726 --> 10:45.102
I only saw the corpses.

10:49.607 --> 10:52.943
We found all the corpses hidden
under the deck of each building.

10:53.027 --> 10:54.403
There are 48 in total.

10:54.820 --> 10:56.072
Load them up on the wagon

10:56.155 --> 10:58.282
- and take them to the magistrate's office.
- Yes, sir.

11:07.833 --> 11:08.668
[sighs]

11:08.751 --> 11:10.044
His corpse is not here.

11:10.461 --> 11:11.295
Pardon?

11:12.171 --> 11:13.923
Physician Lee's corpse is not here.

11:15.132 --> 11:16.175
He must be alive.

11:16.717 --> 11:18.594
- [lively music playing]
- [people chattering]

11:18.678 --> 11:20.846
[man] Is it okay for me to be so happy?

11:20.930 --> 11:23.182
[man 2] How about a little peek?

11:23.265 --> 11:25.142
- [women squealing]
- [men laughing]

11:25.226 --> 11:27.812
Okay, everyone!

11:29.063 --> 11:30.690
Here's to our newly appointed

11:31.273 --> 11:34.026
Magistrate Cho Beom-pal

11:34.610 --> 11:37.613
of the Haewon Cho Clan!

11:38.280 --> 11:39.615
Let's drink to him!

11:39.699 --> 11:41.075
[cheering]

11:41.158 --> 11:43.577
- [Beom-pal] Thank you.
- Hold on!

11:43.661 --> 11:44.704
Wait! Hold on!

11:45.705 --> 11:46.914
[laughing]

11:47.707 --> 11:50.376
- You must have drunk too much!
- Damn it!

11:50.459 --> 11:52.503
- [dishes clatter]
- [laughing]

11:58.384 --> 12:00.177
Let me bow before the magistrate

12:00.261 --> 12:03.264
- on this glorious day.
- Sounds great.

12:03.347 --> 12:04.473
Sure!

12:04.557 --> 12:06.851
May you live long and prosper!

12:06.934 --> 12:08.519
[laughter]

12:10.980 --> 12:13.065
[clerk] My lord!

12:15.192 --> 12:16.986
[clerk] My lord!

12:18.028 --> 12:19.989
- Something terrible happened.
- What?

12:20.656 --> 12:22.658
[suspenseful music playing]

12:23.784 --> 12:25.578
[head clerk] How can I believe you?

12:26.495 --> 12:28.372
[Beom-pal panting]

12:28.956 --> 12:30.332
[men gasping]

12:37.548 --> 12:40.843
[stuttering] What is all this?

12:40.926 --> 12:43.971
[stammering]
Are these all corpses? [gasps]

12:44.054 --> 12:47.808
They were found
in Jiyulheon on Geumjeong Mountain.

12:47.892 --> 12:49.643
[gasps]

12:52.229 --> 12:53.981
Not on my first day in office...

12:56.567 --> 12:59.236
[stammers] What about the culprit?
Do we know who did this?

12:59.779 --> 13:01.322
- There is a suspect.
- [gasps]

13:01.405 --> 13:04.366
A man named Yeong-sin,
who was being treated at the clinic,

13:04.450 --> 13:06.786
has been gathering bamboo poles
from all around Dongnae

13:06.869 --> 13:07.912
for the past few days.

13:07.995 --> 13:10.206
- [stuttering] Did you say--
- Bamboo?

13:10.289 --> 13:13.459
There were bamboo spears
on top of the walls of the clinic.

13:13.542 --> 13:15.544
Bamboo spears? Why?

13:15.628 --> 13:18.798
Probably to keep people out,
so they would not find the corpses.

13:19.632 --> 13:22.009
I checked his identification,
and it belonged to a man

13:22.092 --> 13:23.677
who died in a war three years ago.

13:24.303 --> 13:25.346
[gasps]

13:26.430 --> 13:30.309
That man is suspicious!
Rally up the troops and find him!

13:31.060 --> 13:32.520
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!

13:33.854 --> 13:36.398
What is going on here?

13:36.482 --> 13:37.983
[squeals]

13:39.235 --> 13:41.946
How could something like this happen?

13:42.404 --> 13:43.739
[gasps]

13:43.823 --> 13:46.408
- [man] Please, my lord.
- [man 2] What have I done, my lord?

13:46.492 --> 13:49.370
- [man 3] I did not do anything.
- Talk to the magistrate, not me!

13:50.955 --> 13:54.834
[man 3] I am not who you are looking for.
Please hear me out, my lord.

14:08.430 --> 14:09.807
[Mu-yeong] He is not whom you seek.

14:25.281 --> 14:26.448
What happened?

14:27.074 --> 14:30.244
They are searching for a man
named Yeong-sin, whom they suspect.

14:31.287 --> 14:32.288
What about Physician Lee?

14:32.371 --> 14:36.000
They are too focused
on finding the culprit to think about him.

14:44.425 --> 14:45.509
Where are you going?

14:45.885 --> 14:48.012
I cannot waste time waiting here.

14:49.179 --> 14:50.681
I must find Physician Lee,

14:51.223 --> 14:53.225
even if I must turn Dongnae upside down.

14:53.309 --> 14:54.935
I agree, Your Royal Highness.

14:55.019 --> 14:58.647
We must find that physician so that
I can return to my wife in Hanyang.

14:58.731 --> 14:59.648
Any plan in mind?

15:00.482 --> 15:03.652
Your Royal Highness just said
we shall turn Dongnae upside down.

15:04.320 --> 15:07.156
Dongnae is tiny compared to Hanyang.

15:07.781 --> 15:09.950
It can't be that hard
to find the physician.

15:11.994 --> 15:14.496
[horse neighing]

15:20.336 --> 15:22.046
Giddy up!

15:26.050 --> 15:27.384
[man] We are almost there.

15:27.843 --> 15:29.511
We will split into three groups.

15:30.512 --> 15:33.390
If you see the Crown Prince,
take him to the magistrate's office.

15:33.807 --> 15:35.392
Giddy up. Giddy up.

15:35.476 --> 15:36.810
Giddy up!

15:45.235 --> 15:47.112
GANGNYEONGJEON

15:47.196 --> 15:49.198
[ominous music playing]

16:48.549 --> 16:51.844
[councillor] Where is the covenant
with the Crown Prince's signature?

16:51.927 --> 16:53.053
What do you mean?

16:53.679 --> 16:56.640
Take that covenant to Lord Cho Hak-ju.

16:57.016 --> 16:59.852
Then you can prevent any more deaths
of the scholars.

16:59.935 --> 17:01.061
Have you lost your mind?

17:01.145 --> 17:03.731
His Royal Highness abandoned us and fled.

17:03.814 --> 17:05.482
We must find a way to survive.

17:06.191 --> 17:07.109
[clears throat]

17:07.609 --> 17:08.569
That is enough.

17:09.903 --> 17:12.364
Do you not know why Lord Cho Hak-ju,

17:12.948 --> 17:15.284
who went after the Crown Prince,
is leaving you alone?

17:17.453 --> 17:18.787
He wants you to submit to him.

17:18.871 --> 17:21.206
If you, the head of Sungkyunkwan,

17:21.290 --> 17:24.293
bring all of the scholars
over to the Haewon Cho Clan,

17:24.960 --> 17:27.504
he will at least spare the lives
of the scholars.

17:27.588 --> 17:29.131
That is enough.

17:29.590 --> 17:32.551
My lord, we do not know
when the Royal Army will storm in.

17:34.344 --> 17:36.138
We must hand it over
before it is taken away.

17:36.221 --> 17:37.681
That is the only way we can survive.

17:38.807 --> 17:39.808
[door closes]

17:42.728 --> 17:46.398
[servant] My lord, you have a guest.

17:50.444 --> 17:51.612
Show the guest in.

17:58.535 --> 18:02.706
What brings the head court lady
of the Crown Prince's palace here?

18:05.417 --> 18:06.418
Come in.

18:09.379 --> 18:11.256
A corpse was found in the King's palace?

18:12.466 --> 18:13.717
I cannot believe it.

18:14.093 --> 18:15.469
How could that be possible?

18:16.053 --> 18:17.721
[chief scholar] I feel the same.

18:17.805 --> 18:20.766
Only royalty are permitted
to enter the backyard.

18:21.642 --> 18:23.477
How did you get in?

18:24.770 --> 18:27.856
After hearing that something strange
has been happening in the King's palace,

18:27.940 --> 18:30.275
I risked my life to sneak in to see.

18:31.610 --> 18:32.694
Please believe me.

18:33.529 --> 18:37.199
How could I lie about something
that my life depends on?

18:39.493 --> 18:40.536
I understand.

18:41.578 --> 18:42.746
You may go.

18:53.215 --> 18:55.259
[councillor] This gives us hope.

19:00.305 --> 19:02.307
If what she says is true,

19:02.766 --> 19:05.727
that means something terrible
happened in the King's palace.

19:05.811 --> 19:09.148
Lord Cho Hak-ju hid that from us.

19:11.316 --> 19:12.901
If we find out what happened,

19:13.485 --> 19:16.321
we may be able to destroy
the Haewon Cho Clan.

19:16.405 --> 19:21.410
We may be able to save the scholars,
His Royal Highness, and ourselves.

19:26.290 --> 19:29.209
DONGNAE

19:51.857 --> 19:52.983
May I help you?

19:54.526 --> 19:55.444
Oh...

19:57.279 --> 19:59.698
Are you Kim, the medicinal herb supplier?

20:01.533 --> 20:02.409
I hear...

20:03.577 --> 20:07.122
you supplied medicinal herbs to Jiyulheon.

20:08.248 --> 20:10.667
I know nothing about what happened.

20:11.418 --> 20:13.629
No. We are here about something else.

20:14.671 --> 20:17.758
We are looking for Physician Lee Seung-hui
for something important.

20:17.841 --> 20:19.343
Do you know where he is?

20:20.302 --> 20:23.180
All I did was supply herbs.
I do not know anything.

20:24.223 --> 20:26.433
My apologies, but I am busy.

20:26.516 --> 20:31.313
He is not done talking.
Do the low-class not learn manners?

20:36.360 --> 20:37.486
My elderly father

20:38.362 --> 20:40.739
has not eaten all day
because of all the fuss.

20:41.740 --> 20:43.825
I shall at least bring him some water.

20:45.077 --> 20:46.787
If you wish to flog me, go ahead.

20:47.412 --> 20:48.789
I am going to draw water.

20:56.797 --> 21:00.425
Sorry. My colleague is like that
because he was spoiled as a child.

21:01.051 --> 21:02.302
Please be understanding,

21:03.011 --> 21:04.805
and tell me if you know anything.

21:05.180 --> 21:07.224
I will compensate you generously.

21:08.267 --> 21:09.810
I told you already.

21:10.560 --> 21:13.355
I have not seen him in months.

21:14.439 --> 21:15.440
[sighs]

21:16.942 --> 21:19.861
Anything will do.
Please tell me something.

21:19.945 --> 21:21.363
[coins clanking]

21:23.282 --> 21:24.950
It is for an important matter.

21:25.701 --> 21:27.494
I will not notify the government.

21:30.622 --> 21:31.498
Yesterday,

21:33.500 --> 21:37.504
Seo-bi, a physician at Jiyulheon,
came to see me.

21:38.922 --> 21:40.966
There is a survivor from Jiyulheon?

21:43.385 --> 21:44.928
Where is she now?

21:46.596 --> 21:47.806
I do not know,

21:48.932 --> 21:51.018
but she probably went to Frozen Valley.

21:51.101 --> 21:52.352
She came to me

21:53.437 --> 21:56.606
and asked about
the resurrection plant that grows there.

21:56.690 --> 21:59.026
People say it can bring the dead
back to life.

21:59.651 --> 22:00.944
She was so out of it.

22:02.154 --> 22:03.989
She did not seem normal.

22:05.907 --> 22:07.075
What did you say?

22:07.492 --> 22:09.119
A plant that brings the dead back to life?

22:09.202 --> 22:10.037
Yes.

22:10.954 --> 22:13.540
But there is no such thing in this world.

22:14.541 --> 22:16.084
Where is this "Frozen Valley"?

22:16.793 --> 22:18.795
[ominous music playing]

22:18.879 --> 22:21.173
[Kim] It is called "Frozen Valley"
since it is so cold there

22:21.256 --> 22:23.050
that the water stays frozen
all year round.

22:23.133 --> 22:26.219
I heard it was in Gomi Mountain,
on the north side of Dongnae.

22:28.388 --> 22:30.057
[panting]

22:37.147 --> 22:40.359
Stay here, Your Royal Highness.
I shall go by myself.

22:40.442 --> 22:43.445
No. I am scared to be left alone.

22:43.528 --> 22:46.198
[panting]

22:52.329 --> 22:54.456
[panting]

22:55.957 --> 22:57.709
It already feels like winter here.

23:00.003 --> 23:01.713
Your Royal Highness, stay behind me.

23:03.840 --> 23:04.883
Your Royal Highness!

23:08.470 --> 23:10.222
[wind gusting]

23:13.767 --> 23:15.352
[both panting]

23:16.019 --> 23:18.021
[ominous music playing]

23:20.690 --> 23:22.692
[clinking]

23:23.944 --> 23:26.279
[whispering] Your Royal Highness,
it is dangerous.

23:28.990 --> 23:30.242
[sword rasps]

23:35.080 --> 23:36.331
[clinking continues]

23:48.427 --> 23:50.929
That is what the dead female physicians
at Jiyulheon were wearing.

23:53.807 --> 23:54.724
[clears throat]

23:59.646 --> 24:03.483
Are you Seo-bi,
the physician from Jiyulheon?

24:08.947 --> 24:10.073
Come out.

24:13.827 --> 24:16.037
It is okay. Come out.

24:16.788 --> 24:17.873
[sword rasps]

24:41.188 --> 24:43.064
Where is Physician Lee Seung-hui?

24:46.193 --> 24:48.945
We came all the way from Hanyang
in search of him.

24:49.029 --> 24:50.238
Where is he?

24:52.032 --> 24:53.241
Physician Lee...

24:55.869 --> 24:58.455
could not avoid the disaster.

24:59.664 --> 25:00.874
What do you mean?

25:01.875 --> 25:03.168
Is he dead?

25:08.256 --> 25:09.257
It is...

25:10.717 --> 25:12.010
all because of...

25:13.428 --> 25:15.138
the resurrection plant.

25:16.848 --> 25:18.934
He said that the plant

25:19.768 --> 25:25.148
caused everything that happened
in Hanyang and at Jiyulheon.

25:26.149 --> 25:27.359
What do you mean?

25:28.318 --> 25:32.280
Are you saying the deaths at Jiyulheon
are related to what happened in Hanyang?

25:36.201 --> 25:39.204
How did you know
that the people died at Jiyulheon?

25:41.498 --> 25:43.542
Did you see them?

25:45.544 --> 25:46.586
Yes.

25:48.755 --> 25:51.925
They took the corpses to the magistrate's
office to investigate the incident.

25:54.177 --> 25:57.180
Did you move them out of Jiyulheon?

25:59.558 --> 26:00.767
No.

26:01.935 --> 26:05.021
No. Those people are not dead.

26:05.855 --> 26:06.982
It must be stopped.

26:15.031 --> 26:15.949
Damn it!

26:16.032 --> 26:17.075
Who are you?

26:18.827 --> 26:19.786
Stop!

26:23.748 --> 26:26.167
- [soldier] I asked who you were!
- Where are they?

26:26.918 --> 26:28.670
- Where did they go?
- Why you...

26:28.753 --> 26:29.796
[grunting]

26:29.879 --> 26:31.172
Where are the people

26:32.048 --> 26:33.466
who were here?

26:38.680 --> 26:40.223
[gasps]

26:47.105 --> 26:49.399
What... What happened?

26:51.318 --> 26:53.820
It looks like a beast mauled her,

26:53.903 --> 26:57.449
but the size of the bite marks
is too small

26:58.241 --> 27:00.035
to be those of a tiger or a wolf.

27:01.786 --> 27:04.164
Then was it a fox?

27:05.540 --> 27:06.541
No.

27:08.543 --> 27:10.837
They do not look like
an animal's bite marks.

27:11.755 --> 27:15.342
They match bite marks of a human being.

27:15.800 --> 27:17.594
What? Of a human being?

27:18.219 --> 27:21.014
What? That is absurd.

27:21.765 --> 27:24.142
How could a person bite
another person to death?

27:26.728 --> 27:28.855
[Yeong-sin] Out of my way! Move!

27:32.651 --> 27:34.235
[grunting]

27:35.779 --> 27:38.365
You cannot leave them here!
You must lock them up!

27:39.032 --> 27:42.285
Who are you to create a ruckus
at the magistrate's office?

27:42.369 --> 27:43.828
I am the man

27:44.996 --> 27:46.081
you were looking for.

27:47.290 --> 27:48.750
I saw everything!

27:48.833 --> 27:50.335
These people are not dead!

27:50.418 --> 27:52.087
He looks like the man we seek.

27:52.170 --> 27:54.255
- [Beom-pal] What?
- He is the culprit.

27:55.131 --> 27:56.132
What?

27:56.216 --> 27:58.051
What are you doing? Arrest him!

27:59.010 --> 28:00.762
[grunting]

28:05.975 --> 28:07.185
[grunting]

28:11.648 --> 28:13.108
These people are not dead!

28:13.191 --> 28:15.735
They will soon wake up and attack people!

28:16.444 --> 28:18.029
Please believe me!

28:18.113 --> 28:20.490
Why are you not arresting that lunatic?

28:20.573 --> 28:21.866
Arrest him now!

28:21.950 --> 28:23.159
[shouts]

28:25.704 --> 28:27.747
Oh, my. The corpses will catch on fire.

28:29.833 --> 28:30.709
[grunts]

28:34.212 --> 28:35.964
[grunting continues]

28:42.220 --> 28:43.680
[panting]

28:43.763 --> 28:45.140
[crowd clamoring]

28:47.934 --> 28:48.977
No!

28:51.563 --> 28:52.689
[grunts]

28:57.068 --> 28:59.070
[indistinct chatter]

29:04.367 --> 29:06.119
Where do you think you are going?

29:06.202 --> 29:09.706
[gasps] There is no time.
They will wake up soon.

29:10.165 --> 29:13.501
This wench is insane.
The dead will wake up?

29:13.585 --> 29:15.920
No. It is all true.

29:16.004 --> 29:17.297
What were you saying?

29:18.006 --> 29:20.675
You said that the plant caused something
in Hanyang and at Jiyulheon.

29:21.092 --> 29:25.346
My master said he saved a dead man
in Hanyang with the resurrection plant.

29:26.473 --> 29:28.391
The exact same thing happened
at Jiyulheon.

29:28.475 --> 29:31.728
The dead people came back to life
as monsters.

29:31.811 --> 29:33.772
We must go and stop them!

29:33.855 --> 29:36.858
What were those people who died
and came back to life like?

29:37.400 --> 29:40.445
Did they have a stench
and make sounds of a beast?

29:42.947 --> 29:44.032
That is correct.

29:46.951 --> 29:48.661
Do you have evidence
to prove what you claim?

29:49.287 --> 29:52.916
Physician Lee's journals are kept
in the medicine shed at Jiyulheon.

29:52.999 --> 29:55.043
Everything is written there.

29:55.126 --> 29:59.672
He said if we find the resurrection plant,
we can figure out how to cure the disease.

29:59.756 --> 30:03.426
I came here to find a cure for them.
Please believe me.

30:03.510 --> 30:04.594
I do not have time.

30:04.677 --> 30:08.181
We must go before the sun sets
and prevent any further deaths.

30:10.225 --> 30:11.392
I will go to Jiyulheon.

30:11.851 --> 30:14.354
Go to the magistrate's office with her
and confirm her assertions.

30:14.437 --> 30:16.940
No. How could you believe
a crazy wench and--

30:17.023 --> 30:18.233
It is a grave matter.

30:19.400 --> 30:21.486
Go and confirm whether it is true or not.

30:29.536 --> 30:30.578
Lead the way.

30:38.753 --> 30:39.754
[grunts]

30:42.173 --> 30:43.967
[Chang] Hyah!

31:12.579 --> 31:13.955
[horse neighs]

31:26.217 --> 31:27.886
[ominous music playing]

31:58.374 --> 32:00.418
[Beom-il] Is this what you came for?

32:02.629 --> 32:03.671
[paper thuds]

32:05.256 --> 32:07.675
All the way here to Dongnae?

32:10.553 --> 32:12.680
This is His Majesty's command.

32:15.433 --> 32:17.143
[paper rustling]

32:19.771 --> 32:24.734
"Upon interrogating the 89 scholars
who spread propaganda,

32:25.735 --> 32:27.779
it was uncovered that the mastermind

32:29.238 --> 32:31.199
behind it all was the Crown Prince.

32:31.699 --> 32:34.202
Bring the Crown Prince
to the Royal Investigation Bureau

32:34.285 --> 32:35.954
and get the whole account

32:37.246 --> 32:40.249
of the conspiracy."

32:44.963 --> 32:48.257
I shall obey His Majesty's command
and take you to Hanyang.

32:48.800 --> 32:52.845
I will not bind you since you are
the Crown Prince of this nation.

32:54.639 --> 32:56.140
Please follow me quietly.

32:57.100 --> 32:58.226
[scoffs]

32:59.477 --> 33:00.895
His Majesty's command...

33:03.481 --> 33:05.900
Does this nation truly have a king?

33:06.776 --> 33:08.945
What do you mean?

33:09.362 --> 33:11.739
Why did you call Physician Lee Seung-hui
to Hanyang?

33:12.323 --> 33:15.368
He is the best at treating smallpox.

33:15.451 --> 33:16.786
Then what did he use

33:17.537 --> 33:18.913
the resurrection plant for?

33:20.999 --> 33:23.209
Did my father pass away?

33:26.129 --> 33:29.841
Of course he did not, Your Royal Highness.

33:30.675 --> 33:31.634
His Majesty is...

33:32.552 --> 33:34.303
still alive.

33:35.763 --> 33:36.931
To tell you the truth,

33:37.807 --> 33:39.892
his mental capacity is not exactly there.

33:40.935 --> 33:44.939
However, he will be fine
until the Queen gives birth.

33:48.943 --> 33:50.486
Do you want it that badly?

33:53.656 --> 33:55.950
Do you want to covet power that badly?

33:56.909 --> 34:00.663
Is that why you committed acts that
someone who serves the King must not do?

34:02.457 --> 34:04.125
Do you want it that badly?

34:06.419 --> 34:08.629
What have you done, Your Royal Highness?

34:10.423 --> 34:13.092
You were only lucky to be born
as the son of the King.

34:13.843 --> 34:15.762
You have done nothing.

34:16.304 --> 34:20.349
And yet, you always looked
at my father and me...

34:22.977 --> 34:25.480
with that look you have now.

34:27.231 --> 34:29.984
As if you were saying, "I am different

34:31.402 --> 34:32.862
from you disgusting insects."

34:33.362 --> 34:34.447
[sighs]

34:34.530 --> 34:35.782
You are correct.

34:36.574 --> 34:37.700
You are insects.

34:38.326 --> 34:40.870
You scorned the King and the royal family.

34:41.412 --> 34:43.539
You brought misery upon the people!

34:44.499 --> 34:47.085
That is what you,
the Haewon Cho Clan, have done.

34:48.795 --> 34:50.296
[paper rustling]

34:54.467 --> 34:56.594
You told me to strike you, did you not?

34:58.805 --> 35:00.389
I shall grant your wish today.

35:02.058 --> 35:03.059
[sword rasps]

35:08.606 --> 35:10.441
You said I was simply lucky?

35:11.567 --> 35:12.401
No.

35:13.194 --> 35:14.695
I was chosen.

35:16.197 --> 35:18.783
With the power bestowed upon me
by my father,

35:19.617 --> 35:20.535
I shall...

35:22.954 --> 35:24.789
- punish you.
- [sword rasps]

35:25.331 --> 35:26.290
[tense music playing]

35:26.791 --> 35:28.960
You cannot kill a person with that sword.

35:30.211 --> 35:31.170
[grunts]

35:33.631 --> 35:35.091
[grunting]

35:35.174 --> 35:36.676
[swords clanging]

35:38.719 --> 35:40.054
[grunting continues]

35:55.194 --> 35:56.028
[groans]

36:01.993 --> 36:03.077
[hat thuds]

36:05.830 --> 36:08.249
[both grunting]

36:11.002 --> 36:11.836
[groans]

36:16.632 --> 36:18.551
[both grunting]

36:34.775 --> 36:36.235
- Ahh!
- [swords clang]

36:42.783 --> 36:45.077
You should not have been born
as the Crown Prince.

36:48.164 --> 36:49.165
[thump]

36:50.833 --> 36:51.834
[thumping continues]

36:55.421 --> 36:57.423
[ominous music playing]

36:57.924 --> 36:59.467
[thumping]

37:42.760 --> 37:44.303
[Beom-pal] Confess right now!

37:44.387 --> 37:47.598
- Why did you kill those people?
- Say something!

37:48.015 --> 37:49.892
How many times must I tell you?

37:50.518 --> 37:52.728
They are monsters. They do not die.

37:53.646 --> 37:56.816
We must all flee before the sun sets.

37:57.400 --> 37:58.985
He has lost his mind.

37:59.986 --> 38:01.195
Strike him again!

38:03.948 --> 38:05.950
[indistinct chatter]

38:09.161 --> 38:11.163
[panting]

38:11.747 --> 38:13.082
Excuse me.

38:15.668 --> 38:16.669
- My lord!
- Stop!

38:17.253 --> 38:20.298
Please let me in!
I am a physician at Jiyulheon!

38:25.720 --> 38:26.971
Send her in!

38:31.600 --> 38:33.060
What he speaks is the truth.

38:33.561 --> 38:35.313
These people are not dead.

38:35.938 --> 38:39.108
Once the sun sets,
they will rise and maul people to death.

38:39.775 --> 38:41.777
You must lock them up right away.

38:43.237 --> 38:45.364
[indistinct chatter]

38:45.448 --> 38:47.700
Have they lost their minds?

38:47.783 --> 38:49.327
Please believe me.

38:49.410 --> 38:51.203
You must lock them up quickly.

38:51.287 --> 38:54.206
Otherwise, all the people in Dongnae
will be put in danger.

38:54.290 --> 38:55.708
[panting]

39:01.297 --> 39:02.882
[scoffs, laughs]

39:03.424 --> 39:05.551
You must flee. Hurry!

39:06.177 --> 39:07.386
[men scoff]

39:14.101 --> 39:16.520
Imprison those lunatics
right this instant!

39:16.604 --> 39:17.438
Lock them up!

39:18.022 --> 39:21.609
My lord. My lord!
You must evacuate the people!

39:22.276 --> 39:24.403
You must flee right now!

39:24.487 --> 39:27.490
Flee! You must flee!

39:27.573 --> 39:28.949
[Seo-bi screams]

39:29.033 --> 39:30.368
- Why that...
- [Seo-bi] Run!

39:30.451 --> 39:31.869
She is so loud.

39:33.245 --> 39:35.414
[woman]
Why would we flee from the corpses?

39:42.880 --> 39:43.839
Huh?

39:44.715 --> 39:45.716
It moved.

39:46.884 --> 39:48.719
- [bird hoots]
- [insects chirping]

39:53.599 --> 39:55.601
[ominous music playing]

40:06.070 --> 40:07.154
[clink]

40:45.860 --> 40:47.862
The royal physician was correct.

40:48.821 --> 40:50.114
His Majesty...

40:51.532 --> 40:52.783
has passed away.

40:56.579 --> 40:59.039
Passed away? What are you saying?

41:00.583 --> 41:02.042
His Majesty is alive.

41:11.469 --> 41:12.720
One month from now...

41:14.930 --> 41:18.142
until the Queen gives birth to a prince,

41:19.894 --> 41:21.729
he has to stay alive.

41:22.813 --> 41:25.149
- [Seung-hui] Lord Cho.
- Why are you hesitating?

41:26.734 --> 41:29.153
It is the physician's duty
to save the King.

41:31.280 --> 41:34.533
All you must do is do your duty.

41:37.745 --> 41:39.205
Do not fear anything.

41:41.248 --> 41:43.042
Just do what you did

41:45.544 --> 41:47.421
three years ago.

42:10.069 --> 42:11.654
[ominous music playing]

42:13.197 --> 42:14.698
[chain clatters]

42:15.824 --> 42:17.326
[growling]

42:18.953 --> 42:20.496
[growling intensifies]

42:22.414 --> 42:23.290
[roaring]

42:23.374 --> 42:25.376
[indistinct chatter]

42:31.173 --> 42:32.299
It moved!

42:32.800 --> 42:33.884
What did?

42:34.843 --> 42:36.845
[indistinct chatter]

42:47.356 --> 42:48.941
[all gasp]

42:52.319 --> 42:54.154
[clamoring]

42:58.701 --> 43:01.161
[stuttering] Hey! Hey!

43:02.580 --> 43:05.499
Hey, try lifting that up!

43:06.959 --> 43:08.043
Go on!

43:26.562 --> 43:28.063
- What...
- Why that...

43:28.147 --> 43:29.815
Just use your hand.

43:29.898 --> 43:31.734
Be a man! Why are you such a coward?

43:41.452 --> 43:42.453
[gasping]

43:42.536 --> 43:43.787
Whoa! Whoa!

43:44.580 --> 43:46.290
[mumbling]

44:04.099 --> 44:05.142
Ahh!

44:05.225 --> 44:06.852
[stammering] What is that...

44:09.229 --> 44:10.356
[crowd gasping]

44:10.439 --> 44:12.524
[indistinct chattering]

44:12.608 --> 44:14.943
[gasping, stammering]

44:15.819 --> 44:17.488
- The corpse is...
- [man] Honey!

44:18.155 --> 44:21.617
Honey! Let me go! That is my wife!

44:21.700 --> 44:23.077
She is my wife!

44:23.160 --> 44:25.537
Honey! Darling! Darling!

44:26.413 --> 44:28.040
Honey.

44:28.123 --> 44:30.084
Darling! Darling...

44:30.167 --> 44:32.211
[snarling]

44:32.878 --> 44:34.880
[grunts, screaming]

44:35.547 --> 44:37.424
[snarling intensifies]

44:51.814 --> 44:53.982
[snarling]

44:59.655 --> 45:00.739
[screaming]

45:05.119 --> 45:07.121
[snarling]

45:16.004 --> 45:17.297
[woman screaming]

45:19.216 --> 45:20.843
Ahh! [grunts]

45:22.302 --> 45:23.971
[panting]

45:27.057 --> 45:28.892
[distant clamoring]

45:45.117 --> 45:46.535
- [growling]
- [gasps]

45:48.036 --> 45:49.371
[screaming]

45:56.420 --> 45:57.463
[grunts]

45:58.297 --> 46:00.215
[creature snarling]

46:14.021 --> 46:16.523
- [growling]
- [shouts]

46:21.361 --> 46:22.780
[snarling]

46:22.863 --> 46:25.532
[growling, hissing]

46:29.787 --> 46:31.079
[grunting]

46:37.544 --> 46:38.545
[snarling]

46:48.639 --> 46:49.973
[panting]

46:55.354 --> 46:56.814
[snarling]

47:00.359 --> 47:01.777
[growling]

47:02.778 --> 47:03.862
[grunts]

47:09.243 --> 47:10.577
[growls]

47:10.661 --> 47:12.079
- [screaming]
- [snarling]

47:17.709 --> 47:19.461
[screaming]

47:21.922 --> 47:23.715
[panting]

47:34.935 --> 47:35.978
[groans]

47:48.240 --> 47:51.034
[groaning]

48:00.002 --> 48:01.003
[whimpers]

48:07.426 --> 48:09.344
[clinking]

48:27.029 --> 48:29.031
[ominous music playing]

48:31.867 --> 48:33.952
[growling]

48:38.957 --> 48:41.043
[snarling intensely]

48:48.175 --> 48:50.010
[panting]

48:55.015 --> 48:56.600
- [thud]
- [grunts]

48:59.811 --> 49:01.480
[panting]

49:06.985 --> 49:08.070
[whimpers]

49:12.616 --> 49:14.034
[panting]

49:18.622 --> 49:19.957
[grunting]

49:31.051 --> 49:32.386
[grunting]

49:32.469 --> 49:34.096
[panting]

49:56.034 --> 49:58.036
[theme music playing]

53:48.183 --> 53:49.809
[music ends]
